Likutay Halachos — Birchas HaMazon U'Mayim Acharonim, Halachos 1–2

:root{--bg:#faf8f3;--text:#2c2418;--accent:#8b6914;--accent-muted:#b8a070;--border:#d4c9a8;--translator-bg:#eef3ed;--translator-border:#7a9a6d;--section-num:#6b5a2a;}

*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box;}

body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-family:'EB Garamond','Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.85;padding:2rem 1rem;max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;text-align:justify;}

.book-title{font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;text-align:center;color:var(--accent);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.3rem;}

.halacha-title{font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:600;text-align:center;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:1.8rem;padding-bottom:1rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--border);}

.lm-subtitle{background:#f8f4e8;border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 1.2rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7;border-radius:4px;text-align:center;font-style:italic;color:var(--section-num);}

.sn{font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.3rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);}

.p{margin-bottom:1.5rem;}

.v{font-style:italic;color:#4a3b1f;} .sr{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--accent-muted);font-style:normal;}

.h{font-style:italic;color:var(--accent);}

.lr{font-weight:600;color:var(--accent);} .kc{font-weight:600;}

.mx{font-weight:600;color:#4a3b1f;font-style:italic;}

.sep{text-align:center;margin:2.5rem 0;color:var(--accent);font-size:1.3rem;letter-spacing:.4em;}

.ts{background:var(--translator-bg);border:1px solid var(--translator-border);border-left:5px solid var(--translator-border);border-radius:4px;padding:1.3rem 1.5rem;margin-top:2.5rem;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7;}

.ts .sh{font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--translator-border);margin-bottom:.8rem;text-align:center;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;}

.colophon{margin-top:2.5rem;padding:1.2rem;border:2px solid var(--accent);border-radius:6px;text-align:center;font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--accent);line-height:1.7;}

Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim

Hilchos Birchas HaMazon U'Mayim Acharonim

Halachos 1–2

Halachah 1

Based on LM I:17 ("Vayhi Heim Merikim") and LM I:47 ("Va'Achaltem Achol")

As explained above in Hilchos Netilas Yadayim and Betzi'as HaPas, Halachah 1: eating is the aspect of drawing da'as [holy awareness]. Rabbainu also writes in LM I:17 that through eating, the da'as is completed.

Mayim Acharonim: Sustaining the Da'as
